# openapi — one directory per spec, written by `npm run generate:openapi`, which
# `npm run build` runs before `next build`. These names mirror the SPECS keys in
# lib/openapi/index.ts; add a line here when you add a spec there.
#
# The generator emits BOTH .mdx pages and a meta.json per group, so ignore the directories
# rather than a file extension — ignoring only *.mdx previously left the group meta.json
# files tracked, where they drifted whenever GROUP_META changed and were rewritten in place
# by the jsonSchema plugin on every fumadocs-mdx run.
content/docs/openapi/automation-workflow-execution/
content/docs/openapi/automation-project-code-workflow/
content/docs/openapi/automation-project-git/
content/docs/openapi/embedded-action/
content/docs/openapi/embedded-tool/
content/docs/openapi/embedded-workflow-execution/
content/docs/openapi/embedded-tool-invocation/
content/docs/openapi/embedded-configuration-integration/
content/docs/openapi/embedded-configuration-integration-instance/
content/docs/openapi/embedded-configuration-integration-instance-workflow/
content/docs/openapi/embedded-configuration-connection/
content/docs/openapi/embedded-configuration-connected-user/
content/docs/openapi/embedded-configuration-connected-user-project-workflow/
content/docs/openapi/embedded-configuration-automation-workflow-project/
content/docs/openapi/embedded-webhook-app-event-trigger/
content/docs/openapi/embedded-webhook-request-trigger/
content/docs/openapi/automation-bridge/
content/docs/openapi/custom-components/
# openapi/index.mdx and openapi/meta.json are hand-written and stay tracked.
